invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_exp.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_mont64_exp_schedule
reason: rsa_mont64_public_exp multiplies at the exponent's clear bits and
  not its set ones, so a DNSSEC signature is checked against the wrong
  power. The rsa_mont64_exp_schedule proof asserts one product for each
  set bit, and fails on this edit.

--- old
        if (((e >> i) & 1) != 0) {
--- new
        if (((e >> i) & 1) == 0) {
